# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REFERENCE LISTING -- NOTHING HERE IS ACTIVE.
#
# Every line is commented out on purpose. This file exists so the complete set of
# environment variables the code reads is disclosed in one place; it is not a
# configuration to apply. Copying it to `.env` verbatim therefore sets nothing,
# which is the intended outcome: the defaults compiled into the code are exactly
# what produced the reported result, and the public-set score reproduces with no
# `.env` file at all.
#
# To enable the optional hosted layers, uncomment GROQ_API_KEY and supply a key.
# That is the only line anyone should need to touch. Never commit a real key --
# `.env` is gitignored, `.env.example` is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- the one switch that changes anything ----------------------------------
# Activates the deparaphraser and the transcript rescue, which are flagged on in
# code but inert without a credential. Costs are the key owner's. Omitting it
# changes the public-set score by exactly zero -- both layers are unreachable
# there, because the recognition gate matches every official message.
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- optional hosted layers: already on, shown for disclosure --------------
# LLM_RESOLVE=1          deparaphraser: unattested value -> catalogue-attested
# LLM_RESCUE=1           whole-transcript recovery, once, on a stalled session
# LLM_RESCUE_TURN=5      first turn the rescue may fire
# LLM_RESCUE_REJECTS=4   rejected candidates required before it may fire

# --- local layers: already on, no credential, no network, no per-call cost --
# V2_ROUTE=1             dialogue-act router for unfamiliar wrappers
# BERT_EXTRACT=1         scaffolding tagger, strips filler before mining
# BERT_KEEP=0.30         keep-probability threshold for that tagger

# --- read by the code, but should not be set -------------------------------
# Listed so nothing is undisclosed, not because any of it is needed.
#
# BERT_TAGGER_DIR=       checkpoint directories. Leave unset: resolution already
# V2_ROUTE_MODEL_DIR=    prefers a local directory that actually contains weights
#                        and otherwise uses the Hub, which is what a fresh clone
#                        needs. A path with no weights in it is ignored.
#
# BERT_TAGGER_HUB=KhiemGOM/techjam-scaffolding-tagger   only for mirroring our
# V2_ROUTE_HUB=KhiemGOM/techjam-route-classifier        published checkpoints
#
# BERT_DEVICE=auto       CUDA when present, CPU otherwise. Irrelevant to the
#                        score: the tagger never loads on the public set.
#
# GROQ_MODEL=            DO NOT SET. Each hosted layer picks its own model in
#                        code; this overrides all of them at once and moves them
#                        onto a model they were never measured on.
#
# MESSAGE_VARIETY=1      clarification phrasing variety. Presentation only -- the
#                        simulator reads the structured `ask_attribute`, never the
#                        prose, so it cannot affect scoring.
